{
  "opening": "This release introduces the new TLRU cache algorithm and enhances the key generation utilities with a typed method key decorator. It also adds introspection capabilities to decorators via cache_info and cache_clear, while deprecating the legacy MRUCache implementation.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m01",
      "text": "The library must provide a TLRUCache class that implements the Time-Limited Least Recently Used eviction policy. This class should support standard mapping operations including get, set, pop, and clear."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02",
      "message": "Refactor time aware caches.",
      "public_names": ["RRCache", "TLRUCache", "TTLCache", "clear", "currsize", "get", "pop", "popitem", "setdefault", "timer", "unlink"]
    },
    {
      "id": "m11",
      "text": "Decorators such as @cached and @cachedmethod must expose their configuration parameters (e.g., maxsize, ttl) as attributes on the wrapper function. These attributes should allow inspection of the underlying cache settings without modifying the decorated function's signature."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17",
      "text": "The keys module must export a methodkey function that generates cache keys based on the method name and arguments. This complements existing hashkey and typedkey functions for flexible key generation strategies."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18",
      "text": "Cached functions created by @cached and @cachedmethod must include a cache_clear method. Calling this method must remove all entries from the associated cache instance."
    },
    {
      "id": "m27",
      "text": "The @cached decorator must provide a cache_info function or attribute that returns statistics about the cache usage. This information should include metrics like hits, misses, and current size for monitoring purposes."
    },
    {
      "id": "m65",
      "text": "The keys module must provide a typedmethodkey decorator that creates cache keys considering both the argument types and values. This ensures that methods with different type signatures are cached separately."
    },
    {
      "id": "m69",
      "text": "The MRUCache class is deprecated and should emit a deprecation warning when instantiated or used. Users should migrate to alternative cache implementations provided by the library."
    },
    {
      "id": "m71",
      "text": "The expire method on TTLCache must return an iterable of expired (key, value) pairs. This allows consumers to process or retrieve data from items that have passed their time-to-live threshold."
    },
    {
      "id": "m72",
      "text": "The expire method on TLRUCache must return an iterable of expired (key, value) pairs. This behavior mirrors TTLCache to ensure consistent API interaction for time-aware caches."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure all public APIs behave as described above and that deprecation warnings are properly configured for removed features."
}
